node_modules/
dist/
*.log
.DS_Store

# ANCHORED, and the leading slash is the whole point. Unanchored, `coverage/`
# matches a directory of that name at ANY depth -- which in this repository is
# three of them: `src/shu/coverage/` (the source of the verb that READS
# coverage reports), `src/shu/fixtures/coverage/` and
# `src/schema/fixtures/shu-coverage-repo/coverage/` (38 fixture and source
# files between them). Every one had to be forced past the rule to be
# committed at all, and the next file added beside them would have been
# skipped by `git add .` without a word. What this line exists to ignore is
# the report THIS repository's own test run writes, and that lands in exactly
# one place: the repository root.
/coverage/

# Nen's own generated output. NOT `nen/`, which is committed configuration --
# the one-character difference is the whole boundary: `nen/` holds files a human
# wrote and review reads, `.nen/` holds logs and other disposable output. A
# single directory for both would mean staging a build log by accident.
.nen/

# Hatsu's rikugan reports, written under this repository when Kurapika runs
# here -- final-report output only, never committed configuration.
Reports/

# A read-only bankai-scaffold reference clone used while porting scripts and
# skills into this repository. It is scratch space for the port, not part of
# it -- nothing here is ever imported, and it must never be committed.
.ref/

# `.claude/worktrees/` -- where Kurapika (and every other local agent) checks
# out its own working branch via `git worktree add`, one full checkout per
# effort, each carrying its own `node_modules/`, `dist/` and `coverage/`.
# `worktrees/` ONLY, not the whole `.claude/` directory: nothing under
# `.claude/` is tracked today (`git ls-files .claude` is empty), but a
# committed `.claude/` config -- agent definitions, hooks, skills -- may exist
# here one day the way it already does in hatsu, and this line must not
# pre-emptively ignore it.
.claude/worktrees/

# `bun build --compile` drops a `.<hash>.bun-build` scratch file in the repository
# root while it links the binary. It is build residue, never source.
.*.bun-build
